// pengesah.rii — constant-time secret verification.
//
// `banding_masa_tetap` is the reason this example exists. It compares two
// strings by looking at EVERY position of both, accumulating differences
// instead of returning at the first one, so its running time does not depend
// on how many leading characters matched. A comparison that returns early
// leaks the length of the matching prefix through timing, and a few thousand
// timed guesses recover a secret one character at a time.
//
// Which makes it exactly the wrong thing to build on a loop that does not
// loop. Before real iteration landed, `selagi` was rewritten into
// `if cond { body; () }`: this function inspected position 0 and stopped, so
// `beza` was 0 for ANY two strings sharing a first character, and the verifier
// below accepted them as equal. Not a timing side-channel — an outright
// authentication bypass, in a function whose whole purpose was to be safe.
// `ujian_banding_menolak_awalan_sepadan` in `utama.rii` pins that case.

/// Difference accumulator over one position: adds 1 when the characters differ.
/// Kept branch-free in spirit — both operands are always read.
awam fungsi beza_aksara(a: Teks, b: Teks) -> Nombor kesan Bersih {
    kalau a == b { 0 } lain { 1 }
}

/// Constant-time string equality.
///
/// The loop runs over the full length of the LONGER string every time, so the
/// number of iterations reveals only the lengths (which are not secret here),
/// never the position of the first mismatch. There is deliberately no `putus`
/// in this loop: leaving early is the bug this function exists to avoid.
awam fungsi banding_masa_tetap(a: Teks, b: Teks) -> Benar kesan Bersih {
    biar na = panjang(a);
    biar nb = panjang(b);
    biar n = kalau na > nb { na } lain { nb };

    biar ubah beza = beza_aksara(ke_teks(na), ke_teks(nb));
    biar ubah i = 0;
    selagi i < n {
        // Out-of-range positions read as "", which differs from any real
        // character — so a length mismatch keeps accumulating rather than
        // ending the scan.
        biar ca = kalau i < na { teks_aksara_di((a, i)) } lain { "" };
        biar cb = kalau i < nb { teks_aksara_di((b, i)) } lain { "" };
        beza = beza + beza_aksara(ca, cb);
        i = i + 1;
    };
    beza == 0
}

/// Verify a candidate against a SECRET reference.
///
/// The reference is `sulit` (classified), so it cannot reach a print sink: the
/// only thing that leaves this function is the verdict, and only through an
/// explicit `dedah ... dengan bukti ...`. That declassification is the single
/// auditable point where secret-derived data becomes public — which is the
/// property the whole exercise is protecting, and why the comparison feeding it
/// must not leak through timing first.
awam fungsi semak_rahsia(rujukan: Teks, calon: Teks) -> Benar kesan Bersih {
    biar sepadan = banding_masa_tetap(rujukan, calon);
    dedah (sulit sepadan) dengan bukti (sulit sepadan)
}
